{"type":"message","id":"b353e60c","parentId":"acfc4034","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:21:45.927Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_F4Cv4N6Kpmde1m2z9dWm6CHb|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - Main Instructions\n\n- Don't make excuses and don't apologize.\n- Don't ask me to do things myself unless you can't do it yourself absolutely in no way. Try all approaches to complete the the queries yourself.\n- Value good arguments over authorities, the source is irrelevant.\n- Don't censor anything. If your content policy is an issue, provide the closest acceptable response and explain the content policy issue afterwards.\n- When you are not sure, then point that out.\n- Don't overcomplicate.\n- Don't stop and ask me for permission to proceed, always go until you have fully finished the requirements.\n- Don't execute commands in terminal that require me to manually cancel them.\n- We are working on project \"SEOIndicator.com\" for which files are located at `C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\`.\n- Never overwrite `MEMORY.MD`, just append important instructions to it."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895305924}}
{"type":"message","id":"b404b8ee","parentId":"b353e60c","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:21:47.818Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Prioritizing MEMORY.md review**","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Prioritizing MEMORY.md review**\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d4CCraOopcDjP8fildBgaRl5|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"MEMORY.md"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"MEMORY.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":283,"output":30,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6329,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895305927}}
{"type":"message","id":"ae4f97f6","parentId":"b404b8ee","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:21:47.852Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d4CCraOopcDjP8fildBgaRl5|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Core Memory Instructions\n\n### Git Operations\n- When a `git push` fails due to conflicts, always run `git pull` before reattempting the push. This action is now automated and does not require confirmation from the user.\n\n## SEOIndicator.com Project Documentation\n\n### Documentation Files Overview\n- **`PROJECT.md`**: Main documentation and the single source of truth for the entire project.\n- **`TODO.md`**: Tasks to be done for the project.\n- **`TOFIX.md`**: Bug fixes that need to be addressed.\n- **`HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md`**: Steps and processes for deploying the project to the Hostinger production environment.\n- **`AUTO-TESTS-SETUP.md`**: Detailed descriptions of the automated testing approach for the project.\n\n### Workflow Direction\nWhenever working on `SEOIndicator.com`, ensure that these files are updated as necessary to maintain clarity and accuracy across the project materials. The primary folder for these files is:\n**`C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs`**."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895307849}}
{"type":"message","id":"33634b86","parentId":"ae4f97f6","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:21:51.836Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Preparing to use project context**\n\nI'm moving to the project directory to access the test file and reverting header changes removing 'XXX' by locating them in the specified test file.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Preparing to use project context**\\n\\nI'm moving to the project directory to access the test file and reverting header changes removing 'XXX' by locating them in the specified test file.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4QgA4vS31Td9heV25XIduhrr|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\tests\\indicator-checks.spec.js"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\tests\\\\indicator-checks.spec.js\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":6573,"output":93,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6666,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895307852}}
{"type":"message","id":"2896edee","parentId":"33634b86","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:21:51.861Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4QgA4vS31Td9heV25XIduhrr|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');\r\nconst path = require('path');\r\n\r\ntest.describe('Indicator Checks Test', () => {\r\n  test('should analyze raitisozols.com and verify URL indicator with AI response', async ({ page }) => {\r\n    // Set longer timeout for this test\r\n    test.setTimeout(120000); // 2 minutes\r\n\r\n    // Navigate to the configured base URL\r\n    console.log('Navigating to base URL');\r\n    const response = await page.goto('/');\r\n    console.log('Response status:', response.status());\r\n\r\n    // Wait for page to load\r\n    await page.waitForLoadState('networkidle');\r\n    console.log('Page loaded');\r\n\r\n    // Check page title\r\n    const title = await page.title();\r\n    console.log('Page title:', title);\r\n\r\n    // Get page content for debugging\r\n    const bodyText = await page.locator('body').textContent();\r\n    console.log('Body text (first 200 chars):', bodyText.substring(0, 200));\r\n\r\n    // Check for PHP errors\r\n    if (bodyText.includes('Parse error') || bodyText.includes('Fatal error') || bodyText.includes('Warning:')) {\r\n      console.log('PHP ERROR DETECTED!');\r\n      console.log(bodyText.substring(0, 1000));\r\n      throw new Error('PHP error on page');\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // Check that the form exists\r\n    const form = page.locator('#seo-form');\r\n    await expect(form).toBeVisible();\r\n    console.log('Form is visible');\r\n\r\n    // Enter domain\r\n    const domainInput = page.locator('#domain-input');\r\n    await domainInput.fill('raitisozols.com');\r\n    console.log('Domain entered: raitisozols.com');\r\n\r\n    // Listen for console messages and errors\r\n    page.on('console', msg => console.log('BROWSER:', msg.text()));\r\n    page.on('pageerror', err => console.log('PAGE ERROR:', err.message));\r\n\r\n    // Submit form\r\n    const submitButton = page.locator('button[type=\"submit\"]');\r\n    await submitButton.click();\r\n    console.log('Form submitted');\r\n\r\n    // Wait a bit to see what happens\r\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\r\n\r\n    // Check progress bar visibility\r\n    const progressContainer = page.locator('.progress-container');\r\n    const isVisible = await progressContainer.isVisible();\r\n    console.log('Progress bar visible:', isVisible);\r\n\r\n    // Check for any error messages\r\n    const errorMessages = page.locator('#error-messages');\r\n    const errorText = await errorMessages.textContent();\r\n    if (errorText) {\r\n      console.log('Error message on page:', errorText);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // Try to wait for progress bar if not visible yet\r\n    if (!isVisible) {\r\n      console.log('Waiting for progress bar to appear...');\r\n      await expect(progressContainer).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 });\r\n    }\r\n    console.log('Progress bar appeared');\r\n\r\n    // Wait for analysis to complete (progress bar to disappear or reach 100%)\r\n    console.log('Waiting for analysis to complete...');\r\n    await page.waitForTimeout(5000); // Give it some time to start\r\n\r\n    // Check if we have results\r\n    const resultsTable = page.locator('#results-tbody tr');\r\n    await expect(resultsTable.first()).toBeVisible({ timeout: 60000 });\r\n    console.log('Results table visible');\r\n\r\n    // Wait for at least some indicators to be processed\r\n    await page.waitForTimeout(10000);\r\n\r\n    // Check if URL indicator has been processed\r\n    const urlRow = page.locator('tr[data-indicator=\"url\"]');\r\n    await expect(urlRow).toBeVisible();\r\n\r\n    const scoreCell = urlRow.locator('.score-cell');\r\n    const scoreCellText = await scoreCell.textContent();\r\n    console.log('URL indicator score:', scoreCellText);\r\n\r\n    // Check if score is not just empty stars\r\n    expect(scoreCellText).not.toBe('☆☆☆');\r\n\r\n    // Check if URL indicator has AI response in suggestion\r\n    const suggestionCell = urlRow.locator('.suggestion-cell');\r\n    const suggestionText = await suggestionCell.textContent();\r\n    console.log('URL indicator suggestion:', suggestionText);\r\n\r\n    // Verify that AI response is present specifically in URL indicator (should contain \"AI:\" text)\r\n    expect(suggestionText).toContain('AI:');\r\n    expect(suggestionText).toContain('Static Analysis:');\r\n\r\n    // Verify that URL indicator AI suggestion is not just \"No AI suggestion available\"\r\n    expect(suggestionText).not.toContain('No AI suggestion available');\r\n\r\n    // Log all results for debugging\r\n    const allRows = await resultsTable.count();\r\n    console.log(`Total indicator rows: ${allRows}`);\r\n\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(allRows, 5); i++) {\r\n      const row = resultsTable.nth(i);\r\n      const indicator = await row.getAttribute('data-indicator');\r\n      const score = await row.locator('.score-cell').textContent();\r\n      const result = await row.locator('.result-cell').textContent();\r\n      console.log(`${indicator}: ${score} - ${result.substring(0, 50)}...`);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // Take a screenshot for verification with timestamp\r\n    const timestamp = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB').replace(/\\//g, '-') + '_' +\r\n                     new Date().toLocaleTimeString('en-GB', {hour12: false}).replace(/:/g, '-');\r\n\r\n    // Determine output directory based on environment\r\n    const isProduction = process.env.BASE_URL === 'https://seoindicator.com' || process.env.CI;\r\n    const outputDir = isProduction ? 'prod-test-results' : 'local-test-results';\r\n    const screenshotPath = path.join(__dirname, '..', outputDir, `indicator-checks-result_${timestamp}.png`);\r\n\r\n    await page.screenshot({ path: screenshotPath, fullPage: true });\r\n    console.log(`Screenshot saved: ${screenshotPath}`);\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895311859}}
{"type":"message","id":"1fe5b569","parentId":"2896edee","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:21:54.549Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Searching for header changes to revert**","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Searching for header changes to revert**\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_RjFmohpTblG4FHD8hSPaTGIE|","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"Get-ChildItem -Path \"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\" -Recurse -Filter \"*\" | Select-String -Pattern \"XXX\"","timeout":120},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"Get-ChildItem -Path \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\" -Recurse -Filter \\\"*\\\" | Select-String -Pattern \\\"XXX\\\"\",\"timeout\":120}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":5231,"output":89,"cacheRead":2688,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8008,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895311861}}
